# Global config for drone-stack. Sourced by setup.sh and run.sh.
# Edit paths to match the host. ${VARS} here are usable in module.yml `mounts:`.

# ROS
ROS_MASTER_PORT=11311

# Default build target arch (override per-stack via stacks/*.yml `arch:` or PLATFORM=)
DEFAULT_ARCH=arm64

# Base image (multi-arch). Heavy stages build on top.
BASE_IMAGE=ros:noetic-ros-base-focal

# --- component source: cloned by `setup.sh clone <stack>` into ros_ws/src + livo_ws/src
#     (gitignored, each keeps its own git). risk-aware = main 단일브랜치(2026-07-25 통일,
#     jetson-orin-agx는 main 조상이라 은퇴); fast-livo는 jetson-orin-agx가 정본. ---
RISK_AWARE_REPO=git@github.com:sanghun17/risk-aware_planning.git
RISK_AWARE_BRANCH=main
FASTLIVO_REPO=git@github.com:sanghun17/fast_livo2_custom.git
FASTLIVO_BRANCH=jetson-orin-agx
VRPN_CLIENT_REPO=https://github.com/ros-drivers/vrpn_client_ros.git
VRPN_CLIENT_BRANCH=kinetic-devel
SAFETY_REPO=git@github.com:sanghun17/flight_safety.git
SAFETY_BRANCH=main

# --- external model weights (large binaries, not in the repo) -> /root/risk_aware_assets ---
RISK_AWARE_ASSETS=/home/hmcl/risk_aware_assets
# EPIC_SRC=...                                       # (fill when modularizing lidar-epic)
# LIVOX_DRIVER_SRC=...

# RealSense serial (blank = first device)
RS_SERIAL=
# PX4 / MAVROS FCU
FCU_URL=/dev/ttyTHS0:921600
# OptiTrack (Motive) VRPN server IP — lab mocap PC. Read by optitrack.launch via optenv.
OPTITRACK_SERVER=192.168.50.13

# --- ete-train-* stacks: live risk-aware_planning checkout, direct bind-mount (NOT
#     cloned by `setup.sh clone` -- training iterates on uncommitted WIP config/code,
#     unlike the pinned-branch planner/risk-aware-deploy target). On THIS host, points
#     at the new canonical tree (drone-stack-docker/ws/risk-aware/src/risk_aware_planning),
#     not the retired ~/risk-aware_planning checkout. EDIT to the actual path on a
#     remote host (5090/4090) after rsync -- see docs/ETE_TRAIN_GPU_HOSTS.md for the
#     migration checklist (what to rsync, how much, in what order). ---
# ⚠ 2026-07-25: ete-train-* 는 더 이상 이 변수를 쓰지 않는다. training/ete-net 에
#   clone.sh 가 생겨 fast-livo 등과 같은 방식으로 ws/ 에 git clone 하고, dsd 루트가
#   /work 로 마운트되므로 코드 마운트가 불필요해졌다. 남은 소비자는
#   planner/risk-aware-sim 하나뿐이며(그 모듈도 clone.sh 가 없어 같은 구조 문제를
#   갖는다 — 정리 대상), sim 스택이 보존 상태라 이번엔 손대지 않았다.
RISK_AWARE_PLANNING_SRC=/home/ml/drone-stack-docker/ws/risk-aware/src/risk_aware_planning
# ete-train-* data mount (separate from code, see modules/training/ete-net/module.yml):
# UPDATED 2026-07-25 (정본 레이아웃 통합) -- points at /home/ml/data, the DATA_MAP.md
# canonical root (raw/stage1/stage2 tiers), NOT a single flat uncertainty_predictor/data/
# dir anymore. module.yml mounts this whole tree and sets container DATA_ROOT to match,
# so ete_train_config.yaml's ${DATA_ROOT}/data_final etc. keys now resolve under the new
# tiered paths (e.g. stage2/...) -- any config key whose path doesn't exist there halts
# loudly (no fallback), by design. Move this one line if the data is ever relocated again.
ETE_DATA_DIR=/home/ml/data

# GPU_UUIDS (optional): comma-separated GPU UUIDs (`nvidia-smi -L`) to pin an amd64
# ete-train-* container to, instead of the default "any one GPU" (`count: 1`)
# reservation. Needed on the ml desktop itself (ete-train-2080ti) -- it has a dead/
# NVML-broken card at PCI bus 1A:00.0 mixed in with the usable 2080 Ti's, and a bare
# `count: 1` reservation can hit that dead card or error outright. Left BLANK here
# deliberately: which UUID you want changes per gate/run (see
# docs/ETE_TRAIN_GPU_HOSTS.md's 2080ti validation section) -- export it in your shell
# before `./setup.sh {gen,build,up}` instead of hardcoding one value in this
# shared/tracked file, e.g.:
#   GPU_UUIDS=GPU-5f5e6979-51fc-3166-7a87-4e264c81e4dc ./setup.sh up ete-train-2080ti
# GPU_UUIDS=

# CONTAINER_USER (optional, amd64 ete-train-* stacks only, "uid:gid"): confirmed
# 2026-07-14 on a real ete-train-2080ti run -- without this, training writes
# checkpoints/tensorboard/consolidated-cache files into the bind-mounted outputs/ +
# data/ dirs as ROOT-owned (container has no USER directive, defaults to root), which
# the host user then can't delete/overwrite without sudo. Set to your host UID:GID
# (`id -u`:`id -g`) -- on this ml desktop that's 1000:1000. Left unset by default
# (same reasoning as GPU_UUIDS above -- host-specific, don't hardcode one value in
# this shared file):
#   CONTAINER_USER=1000:1000 GPU_UUIDS=... ./setup.sh up ete-train-2080ti
# CONTAINER_USER=

# --- sim-x86 (AirSim/UE4 simulator on the ml desktop, amd64/sm75) ---
# fast-livo `ml` branch (mapping_simulator_openvins.launch, diverged from the
# jetson-orin-agx-pinned FASTLIVO_BRANCH above -- see modules/odometry/fast-livo-sim's
# module.yml). Repo is the same FASTLIVO_REPO.
FASTLIVO_SIM_BRANCH=ml
# model weights, sim-x86 own key (NOT a RISK_AWARE_ASSETS override -- that key stays
# the jetson deploy path above, planner/risk-aware-deploy's mount; verified nothing but that
# one module.yml reads RISK_AWARE_ASSETS, so overwriting it here would silently break
# a future jetson generation run on a host that shares this tracked file). Confirmed
# present on this host (ml desktop) via `ls`, 2026-07-25.
SIM_RISK_AWARE_ASSETS=/home/ml/risk_aware_assets
# GPU UUIDs for sim-x86 (stacks/sim-x86.yml `gpu_uuids_env: SIM_GPU_UUIDS` -- see
# tools/gen_dockerfile_compose.py's gpu_uuids_key param). Fixed here (unlike the
# shared GPU_UUIDS above, which is deliberately left blank/export-at-invocation)
# because sim-x86 always wants the SAME pair on THIS host: phys0,1, byte-identical to
# the host tmux_common.sh's CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES="0,1" + ours_jax.launch gpu:=1
# wiring it replaces (orchestrator-confirmed 2026-07-25, no live nvidia-smi re-check).
SIM_GPU_UUIDS=GPU-5f5e6979-51fc-3166-7a87-4e264c81e4dc,GPU-8149eb0b-023a-17dd-b942-c622f0b8c4ca

# --- compute/torch source-built ABI=1 wheel archive (host-local, 274MB, git-untracked
#     -- see modules/compute/torch/wheels/README.md) ---
# Canonical per-host archive dir the wheel is fetched/hardlinked FROM by
# modules/compute/torch/wheels/stage_from_archive.sh before building any stack that
# sets `build_env: {TORCH_VARIANT: src-abi1}` (sim-x86 today; ete-train-4090-abi1 is a
# 2026-07-26 test stack exploring the same variant for ete-train, see
# docs/ETE_TRAIN_GPU_HOSTS.md). The archive path itself is host-specific (this repo is
# checked out on multiple machines with different disks) -- tracked default below is
# THIS host (ml)'s own copy; override per-host via `config/stack.env.local` instead of
# editing this line (see the per-host-override note at the bottom of this file --
# ETE_DATA_DIR already hit the exact pull-conflict this avoids).
TORCH_WHEEL_ARCHIVE_DIR=/home/ml/risk_aware_assets/wheels_x86

# --- per-host override (untracked) -------------------------------------------
# 이 파일은 추적된다. 호스트마다 다른 값(데이터 경로, GPU UUID 등)을 여기에 직접
# 고치면 그 체크아웃이 영구히 dirty 해지고 pull 마다 충돌한다 — im(pull-only)이
# ETE_DATA_DIR 한 줄 때문에 정확히 이 상태였다(2026-07-26).
# 대신 옆에 `stack.env.local` 을 만들어라(.gitignore 됨). 아래 한 줄이 그걸 읽고,
# 나중에 읽히므로 위의 값을 덮어쓴다. 예:
#   echo 'ETE_DATA_DIR=/media/im/ETE4090/data' > config/stack.env.local
# 셸 소비처(setup.sh, 컨테이너 안 optitrack/mavros run.sh)는 이 줄 덕에 수정이 필요
# 없다. 파서 쪽(tools/gen_dockerfile_compose.py)만 .local 을 따로 먼저 읽는다.
# (이 줄에 "=" 가 없어야 그 파서가 건너뛴다 — 형태를 바꾸지 말 것.)
# `if/fi` 형태 필수 — `[ -f X ] && . X` 를 마지막 줄로 두면 X 가 없을 때(.local 없는
# 대부분의 호스트) 그 `&&` 리스트의 종료 상태가 1 이 되고, source 는 "그 파일에서 마지막
# 실행된 명령의 종료 상태" 를 그대로 돌려주므로 이 source 호출 자체가 1 을 반환한다.
# setup.sh 는 최상단이 `set -euo pipefail` 이라 그 실패가 즉시 스크립트를 죽인다 —
# 에러 메시지 하나 없이. 모든 서브커맨드(gen/build/up/clone/run/sh/down)가 stack.env 를
# source 하는 시점에 걸리므로 .local 이 없는 호스트에서는 setup.sh 전체가 먹통이 된다
# (2026-07-26 dsd_hosts_cross_check 로 ml 에서 실증). `if` 문은 조건이 거짓이어도 그 자체
# 종료 상태가 0 이라 이 문제가 없다.
if [ -f "${BASH_SOURCE[0]%/*}/stack.env.local" ]; then
  . "${BASH_SOURCE[0]%/*}/stack.env.local"
fi
